## BEAM distribution config (env-var driven for cluster deployments).
##
## Defaults make the image work standalone (single-node, default cookie).
## Cluster deployments must set NODE_NAME and RELEASE_COOKIE in the
## environment (same RELEASE_COOKIE on every cluster node).

## Long node name. Format: NAME@HOSTNAME. Hostname must resolve from
## peers; in container deployments use network_mode: host so the
## host's hostname is reachable on the lab subnet.
-name ${NODE_NAME}

## Cookie for distributed Erlang. MUST match on every peer to form
## a cluster. Treat as a secret (it's the only auth between BEAM
## dist nodes).
-setcookie ${RELEASE_COOKIE}

## Hidden-node flag for multi-cluster catalogue mode.
##
## When set to the literal string `-hidden`, the BEAM starts as a
## hidden dist node: it does NOT appear in peers' nodes/0 lists and
## connections to it are non-transitive. Required for clean operation
## when federating cookie-disjoint clusters from one gateway (the
## docs-prescribed pattern; OTP pg sync uses net_kernel:monitor_nodes(true)
## which filters hidden nodes, so each cluster's pg scope stays
## isolated from the others through the gateway bridge).
##
## When empty (default), the gateway runs as a regular visible dist
## node. Required when running an embedded reckon-db store in
## STORE_MODE=cluster, where gateway containers are peers of each
## other in a Ra quorum and MUST be mutually visible for pg sync.
##
## There is no smart default; operators set RECKON_GATEWAY_DIST_HIDDEN_FLAG
## explicitly to `-hidden` for catalogue (or embedded-single) mode,
## or leave it empty for cluster mode. See docs/env-contract.md.
${RECKON_GATEWAY_DIST_HIDDEN_FLAG}

## Increase process limit
+P 1048576

## Increase port limit
+Q 65536

## Distribution buffer
+zdbbl 32768
